{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBSKeZ3RNEJqAsrZci8P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I finished the campaign and submitted index 14 (Ca 0.77, Mn 0.23) as the best composition. It gave the highest photocurrent I measured, 3.0e-7 A.\n\nAll 3 photocurrent measurements went on three points along the composition line:\n\n| Index | Ca fraction | Photocurrent (A) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 26 | 0.22 | −1e-8 (about zero) |\n| 3 | 0.50 | 1.7e-7 |\n| 14 | 0.77 | 3.0e-7 |\n\nPhotocurrent rose steadily as calcium increased.\n\nI used all 5 XRD scans too (Ca 0.13, 0.22, 0.37, 0.50 and 0.78). Every sample has the same main peak. Starting somewhere between Ca 0.22 and 0.37, a second phase shows up and stays up to Ca 0.78, which matches where the photocurrent turns on.\n\nThe most Ca-rich sample in the library is index 13 (Ca 0.78), just past index 14. I didn't measure it, so I can't rule out that it's slightly better. Nor can I say whether the photocurrent peaks somewhere between Ca 0.50 and 0.77 rather than still climbing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_read_input_tokens":8668,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":494},"output_tokens":414,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41c276ad-d26e-4bc7-8e80-744410d81e9b","uuid":"9a43fc53-1615-4600-a0af-d35e9c635271","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:13:30.148Z","request_id":"req_011CfBSKe2XucU7GDvvoK74i"}
